# Integers beyond machine integers in the standard library

Indexes and decimal positions beyond 64 bits are out of range: they must not be
truncated to a small machine integer, and rounding does not compute powers of
ten larger than needed.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope LargeIntegers:
  output nth content optional of integer
  output removed content list of integer
  output money_coarse content money
  output money_fine content money
  output decimal_exact content decimal
  output decimal_coarse content decimal
  output decimal_half content decimal

scope LargeIntegers:
  definition nth equals List.nth_element of [7; 8; 9], 18446744073709551617
  definition removed equals
    List.remove_nth_element of [7; 8; 9], 18446744073709551617
  definition money_coarse equals
    Money.round_to_decimal of $123.45, -18446744073709551616
  definition money_fine equals
    Money.round_to_decimal of $123.45, 18446744073709551616
  definition decimal_exact equals
    Decimal.round_to_decimal of 0.125, 18446744073709551616
  definition decimal_coarse equals
    Decimal.round_to_decimal of 123.45, -18446744073709551616
  definition decimal_half equals
    Decimal.round_to_decimal of 0.125, 2
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope LargeIntegers
┌─[RESULT]─ LargeIntegers ─
│ nth = Absent
│ removed = [
│             7;
│             8;
│             9;
│           ]
│ money_coarse = $0.00
│ money_fine = $123.45
│ decimal_exact = 0.125
│ decimal_coarse = 0.0
│ decimal_half = 0.13
└─
```
